IC Hack Macro Pad Doom port

Apply this patch to Smallest Doom at e176ccb7a444e686b0fd6eb9c31ba09627d14157.
https://github.com/GorGylka/Smallest-Doom

Verified with Pico SDK 98a542c1a62fb549ffb5d66a3e5892b06276b670 and Pico Extras 52fd7a786ce47c989afeaee67e0c6aebee56ed2d.
Run from the patched checkout with the ARM cross-compiler and picotool on PATH.

  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=MinSizeRel -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 \
    -DPICO_BOARD=pico2 -DPICO_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES=2097152 -DPICO_NO_PICOTOOL=1 \
    -DPICO_SDK_PATH="$PICO_SDK_PATH" -DPICO_EXTRAS_PATH="$PICO_EXTRAS_PATH"
  cmake --build build --target doom_tiny --parallel
  picotool uf2 convert -t elf build/src/doom_tiny.elf build/ichack-doom.uf2

The patch uses the upstream doom1.whx shareware data verbatim. The build disables audio and embeds the data at 0x1002f000.

The PlatformIO upload target packs the keyboard and Doom together. To regenerate its Doom payload, replace firmware/doom/doom_tiny.bin with build/src/doom_tiny.bin from this build.

Run from the macropad repository root with the board in BOOTSEL mode.

  pio run -d firmware -e ichack -t upload

Hold H and K during reset to start Doom. Reset with both released to return to the keyboard.

